{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>Into storehouses (לִקְמָצִים)</b> — handful upon handful, hand upon hand, they gathered into storehouses; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 41:47). And the Targum of Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 41:47) renders \"לְאוֹצְרִין\" (into treasuries), for pits dug in the earth for storage or for other things are called קְמָצִים. \"בְּאַחַת הַפְּחָתִים\" (2 Samuel 17:9) — Jonathan translated it \"בַּחֲדָא מִן קֻמְצַיָּא\" (in one of the pits), and likewise every instance of פַּחַת (pit) (Isaiah 24:17, 18) he translates as \"קֻמְצָא\" (pit). And it is close to \"חוֹפֵר גּוּמָּץ\" (Ecclesiastes 10:8), for the letter גִּימֶ\"ל serves here like the letter קוּ\"ף, just as it serves like the letter כָּ\"ף in \"אַל יֶחְסַר הַמָּזֶג\" (Song of Songs 7:3), from \"מָסְכָה יֵינָהּ\" (Proverbs 9:2); \"וְכַנָּה אֲשֶׁר נָטְעָה יְמִינֶךָ\" (Psalms 80:16), which is like \"גַּנָּה\" (Isaiah 1:30); \"וַיִּסָּכְרוּ מַעְיְנֹת תְּהוֹם\" (Genesis 8:2) with the same sense as וַיִּסָּגְרוּ (were closed); \"עַל אֶרֶץ מְכוּרָתָם\" (Ezekiel 29:14) and \"מְכֹרֹתַיִךְ וּמוֹלְדוֹתַיִךְ\" (Ezekiel 16:3); \"וְסִכַּרְתִּי אֶת מִצְרַיִם\" (Isaiah 19:4) — the כָּ\"ף and the גִּימֶ\"ל are equivalent in these, and the קוּ\"ף and the כָּ\"ף are always equivalent, as in \"קוֹבַע\" (1 Samuel 17:38) and \"וְכוֹבַע\" (Ezekiel 27:10); \"תִּקֵּן מְשָׁלִים הַרְבֵּה\" (Ecclesiastes 12:9), like \"מִי תִכֵּן אֶת רוּחַ ה'\" (Isaiah 40:13). And our Sages say it is from the root קִשּׁוּט — ornaments (Shabbat 63a), and תְּקַשֵּׁט (Jerusalem Peah 8:8 / Jerusalem Ketubot 5:3). And likewise \"וַיַּצִּקוּ אֶת אֲרוֹן הָאֱלֹהִים וַיַּעַל אֶבְיָתָר עַד תֹּם כָּל הָעָם לַעֲבֹר מִן הָעִיר\" (2 Samuel 15:24) — the Targum rendered it \"וַאֲקִימוּ יָת אֲרוֹנָא\" (and they set up the Ark), treating it like \"וַיַּצִּיגוּ\" (and they set it down), in the same sense as what is said of it (2 Samuel 6:17), \"וַיָּבִאוּ אֶת אֲרוֹן ה' וַיַּצִּגוּ אֹתוֹ בִּמְקוֹמוֹ\" — from the root of \"אַצִּיגָה נָּא עִמְּךָ\" (Genesis 33:15), \"וְהִצַּגְתִּיו לְפָנֶיךָ\" (Genesis 43:9)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {0 "The Jerusalem Talmud citation is given as ירושלמי כתובות פ\"ו ה\"ג; I rendered it as Jerusalem Peah 8:8 / Jerusalem Ketubot 5:3 since the verb תְּקַשֵּׁט appears in both and the manuscript reference may point to either. The citation 'שבת סג' is resolved as Shabbat 63a, following standard abbreviation of folio side."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:44:02.547212653Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}